          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#in_quantum_field_theory In quantum field theory
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            an
            %em instanton
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} field configuration
            with a “topological twist”: not in the connected component of the trivial field configurations. Specifically for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            which mathematically are represented by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            (or similarly non-trivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+bundle"} associated
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
          %p
            The term derives from the special case of instantons on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            but modeled as field configurations on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            constrained to vanish asymptotically. These look like solutions localized in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            Instantons enter the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axial+anomaly"} axial anomaly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+anomaly"} chiral anomaly
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            which is thought to be a source of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryogenesis"} baryogenesis
            in the early universe. Generally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            state is argued to consist of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superposition"} superposition
            of all possible instanton sectors, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD+instanton"} QCD instanton
          %h3#in_string_theory In string theory
          %p
            More generally, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            which wraps a completely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacelike"} spacelike
            cycle in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is called an
            = succeed "," do
              %em instanton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of such a brane is localized in the
            = succeed "-direction" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time"} time
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+quantum+field+theory"} effective quantum field theory
            of the string theory, this reproduces many instantons in the sense of quantum field theory above.
